          "text": "The restriction reaches new oil sands construction, financed directly, and mostly for that purpose.\n\nExisting operations are outside it: financing to operate, expand by debottlenecking or extend the life of an existing oil sands mine or pipeline is not construction of new assets. Financing only partly for oil sands is outside it, because “wholly or primarily” has no number.\n\nThe definitions narrow it again. Processing means in-situ upgrading by Canadian clients only, and pipelines count only if their primary use is oil sands crude.\n\nWhat remains is earmarked financing to build a new oil sands asset."
